            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/478856?u=efbc4deb51e7378936b0bca66d7da6a08279e86d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds a note that the Japanese calendar doesn't actually at present work correctly in browser for dates before 1868-10-23.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Helps readers avoid triggering a cross-browser bug.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See <a href=\"https://unicode-org.atlassian.net/browse/CLDR-11375\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://unicode-org.atlassian.net/browse/CLDR-11375</a> (linked from the text of the PR) for the bug that causes all browsers to have incorrect data for the start of the Meiji era.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also, see <a href=\"https://tc39.es/proposal-intl-era-monthcode/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://tc39.es/proposal-intl-era-monthcode/</a> , which requires browsers to use Gregorian eras for the Japanese calendar for dates before the Meiji era.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41420",
            "title": "Document that the Japanese calendar is currently broken in browsers for dates before 1868-10-23",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-09T09:04:07.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-07T09:10:34.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hsivonen",
                "url": "https://github.com/hsivonen"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105991?u=9117b059ac229cd023e2188900da14bde6d83fa4&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adding a note for position-try-fallbacks to explain that the element does not revert to its original position when available space is restored.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Developer's intuition for how anchor positioning fallbacks works does not match the specced behaviour, as demonstrated in <a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@Meyerweb/115106404124445073\" rel=\"nofollow\">this poll</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The spec is not expected to change - <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3367549498\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12682\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12682/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12682\">w3c/csswg-drafts#12682</a> - so a note to developers can help prevent the pitfall of not understanding why it's not going back to the starting position.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41419",
            "title": "Add note for anchor positioning fallbacks behaviour",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-07T16:55:23.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-07T09:01:57.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "djmarland",
                "url": "https://github.com/djmarland"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR is part of a series in which I update the Learn area \"Challenge\" articles. In general, they need to be modernized, restructured, and put in better positions in the modules so they are spaced out better and test subjects that have already been covered.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Specifically, this PR adds a new challenge that tests the reader's knowledge of form, table, and media styling.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note\" dir=\"auto\"><p class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"><svg class=\"octicon octicon-info mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z\"></path></svg>Note</p><p dir=\"auto\">This PR still needs to be updated to include the correct image URLs, once <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3487943178\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/shared-assets/issues/71\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/shared-assets/pull/71/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/shared-assets/pull/71\">mdn/shared-assets#71</a> has been merged.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41414",
            "title": "Add challenge to test media, form, and table styling",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-07T08:20:51.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-07T08:16:29.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
