        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This updates the TrustedScriptURL documentation for <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLScriptElement/src\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLScriptElement/src</code></a> to include information about using it with trusted types.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I don't know why/when it would ever make sense to do take an untrusted string, and if you did, to use trusted types. I've presented this primarily as \"Use CSP to restrict the script options but if you have to take and untrusted script then you can use TT\".</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Project tracking in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2770544982\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37518\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/37518/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/37518\">#37518</a></p>",
